[57.094, "o", "   {\"advice\":\"One good change this week: take a 10-minute easy walk after one meal each day, then build it up slowly. Since your region is hazy, do it indoors or at a mall/CC instead of outdoors. Keep it comfortable - you should still be able to talk in short sentences. Also, because your screening risk is High, please follow up with a doctor about your result.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\",\"lg-06-exercise-by-condition\",\"lg-08-screening-schedule\",\"lg-09-hazy-day-activity\",\"lg-10-active-after-60\",\"lg-02-physical-activity-guideline\"],\"rationale\":\"You are 60-64, have elevated blood glucose, low current steps, and a hazy North region. The guides support a gentle after-meal walk, gradual build-up, and indoor alternatives on hazy days. High screening risk also means you should not ignore the result and should follow up with a health professional.\",\"personalisation_flags\":[\"age_60_64\",\"elevated_blood_glucose\",\"high_screening_risk\",\"low_steps\",\"low_mvpa\",\"region_north\",\"region_hazy\",\"disengaged\"]}\r\n"]
