[104.578, "o", "   {\"advice\":\"For next week in Woodlands, I'd suggest these hazy-day-safe morning options: Tue 8:30am Morning Chair Strength & Balance at Woodlands CC, Thu 9:00am Low-Impact Aerobics for Beginners at Woodlands Sport Centre, Sat 8:00am Indoor Mall Walking Club at Woodlands Civic Centre, or Sat 9:30am Diabetes Prevention Programme intake session. They are all indoors and suit your pre-diabetes risk. Start with the lighter ones if you want to build up gently.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-09-hazy-day-activity\",\"lg-06-exercise-by-condition\",\"lg-10-active-after-60\",\"lg-02-physical-activity-guideline\",\"lg-11-faq\"],\"rationale\":\"You're 60-64, in the North/Woodlands area, your region is hazy, and your profile shows elevated blood glucose with low daily steps and low MVPA. The guides suggest indoor or lower-intensity options on hazy days, and for pre-diabetes to start low, go slow, and include regular walking plus strength work. I also matched your morning preference and avoided swimming.\",\"personalisation_flags\":[\"age_60_plus\",\"north_region\",\"woodlands_planning_area\",\"hazy_region\",\"elevated_blood_glucose\",\"low_steps\",\"low_mvpa\",\"morning_preference\",\"dislikes_swimming\"]}\r\n"]
