[198.453, "o", "   {\"advice\":\"For pre-diabetes, keep meals steady and balanced: use the healthy plate, with half vegetables, one quarter wholegrains or other staples, and one quarter protein. Choose brown rice, oats, wholemeal bread or wholegrain noodles more often. Pair rice, noodles, bread or fruit with fish, chicken, tofu, eggs or beans. Spread carbohydrates through the day, avoid skipping meals or crash diets, and swap sugary drinks for water, kopi kosong, teh siew dai, or other less sweet options. At hawker stalls, ask for less gravy/sauce and add vegetables. Please follow up with a doctor or dietitian for personal advice because your blood glucose result is high.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\",\"lg-01-healthy-plate\",\"lg-04-salt-and-sugar-tips\",\"lg-03-nutri-grade\",\"lg-08-screening-schedule\"],\"rationale\":\"You shared elevated blood glucose, so the pre-diabetes guide applies. It recommends the healthy plate pattern, higher-fibre carbohydrates, regular meal timing, and less sweet drinks. The screening guide also says a high blood glucose result should be followed up with a health professional. I used your profile to keep this practical for a 60-64 year old in Woodlands with a hazy regional flag, but the food advice itself does not need haze-specific changes.\",\"personalisation_flags\":[\"age_band:60-64\",\"condition:elevated blood glucose\",\"screening_risk:High\",\"region:North/Woodlands\",\"hazy_region:true\",\"prefers_mornings\",\"dislikes_swimming\",\"weekly_sim...\r\n"]
[198.453, "o", "      [PASS ] lab1_prediabetes_eat on the Fabric coach: no Fabric call -- ['get_citizen_profile', 'memory:search_call', 'knowledge_base_retrieve', 'memory:search_call']\r\n"]
[198.469, "o", "      [PASS ] lab1_prediabetes_eat on the Fabric coach: answered from the guides (knowledge base or Nutrition specialist) -- ['get_citizen_profile', 'memory:search_call', 'knowledge_base_retrieve', 'memory:search_call']\r\n"]
[250.875, "o", "   [livewell-test-coach v2] 51.7s  tools: get_citizen_profile, memory:search_call, DataAgent_Resident360_Ontology_Agent, find_activities, memory:search_call  model: gpt-5.4-mini\r\n"]
[250.875, "o", "   {\"advice\":\"For your age band 60-64, the programme people stick with best is Active Ageing: 28 enrolled, 5 dropped out, so the drop-out share is lowest at 17.9%. At Woodlands, the best start nearby is the Diabetes Prevention Programme: Intake Session at Woodlands Community Club on Sat 09:30. It's indoor and hazy-day safe. If you want, I can help you compare that with the other nearby options before you sign up.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\"],\"rationale\":\"Resident is 60-64, has elevated blood glucose and is in Woodlands with hazy regional context. Fabric shows Active Ageing has the lowest drop-out share in their age band. Nearby indoor intake session for a condition-friendly programme is available at Woodlands, which fits a practical restart after dropping out of Healthier SG.\",\"personalisation_flags\":[\"age_band_60-64\",\"planning_area_Woodlands\",\"region_North\",\"hazy\",\"elevated_blood_glucose\",\"high_screening_risk\",\"dropped_Healthier_SG\",\"low_steps\",\"low_MVPA\",\"disengaged\"]}\r\n"]
